<p>Decimal 36864. Default value: 12 (PAL), 5 (NTSC). Also known as <strong>VICCR0</strong>.</p>
<p>This register has two functions:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bit 7</strong> - selects interlace scan mode for the display.</li>
<li><strong>Bits 6-0</strong> - the distance from the left hand side of the TV picture to the first column of characters.</li>
</ul>
<p>Changing bits 6-0 moves the whole display sideways rather than scrolling the
characters inside it, so it is an easy way to shake the screen or to centre the
picture. Values far from the default push the display off the visible area.</p>

<p>Example</p>
<code>
// nudge the whole screen one step to the right
HSCROLL_REGISTER := 13;
</code>
<p>See also VSCROLL_REGISTER ($9001) for the vertical equivalent.</p>
